expansion technique with cross-validation.  The final concept is of t~~
he form:~
~
     sum ( Kern_i (x), I )~
~
where each Kern_i(x) is a non-linear function.  The basic idea is to ~~
fit a non-linear function (a kernel) to the current residual, thus re~~
ducing the residual, and repeat, reducing the residual on the trainin~~
g data at each iteration.~
~
As kernels are added, the error on a separate cross-validation set is~~
 measured.  At a certain point, the "optimal" number of kernels are i~~
dentified, after which additional kernels over-fit the data and the e~~
rror on the cross-validation set deterioriates with more kernel funct~~
ions.  Hence, the performance on the cross-validation set provides th~~
e mechanism to determine the optimal number of kernel functions.Author: Lonnie Chrisman, Ph.D.~
Lumina Decision SystemsDate: Thu, Nov 15, 2007 9:10 AMSaveauthor: LonnieSavedate: Thu, Nov 15, 2007 3:07 PMDefaultsize: 48,24Diagstate: 1,49,19,605,645,17Windstate: 2,261,365,492,465Fontstyle: Arial, 15Fileinfo: 0,Model Cross_validation_exa,2,2,0,0,W:\TestModels\cross-val~~
idation example.anaModule Empirical_dataTitle: Empirical dataDescription: This model creates the "empirical" data used.  This data ~~
